# Nothing reads this file directly. It exists so a newcomer knows where real
# config lives:
#   - Per-service runtime config: apps/<service>/.env (gitignored)
#   - Deployment config:          deploy/gcp/.env.example
#
# Never commit real values. `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored; this
# `.env.example` (and `deploy/gcp/.env.example`) are the only tracked variants.

# ---- Postgres (Supabase) ----
# One Supabase project per service: core, products, transactions, reports.
# Each service needs two connection strings:
#   <SERVICE>_DATABASE_URL - pooled (Supavisor), port 6543, used at runtime
#   <SERVICE>_DIRECT_URL   - direct, port 5432, used ONLY by Prisma Migrate
# Why both: Supavisor's transaction mode can hand a different backend
# connection to each transaction, which breaks the session-scoped advisory
# locks Prisma Migrate takes, so migrations must run on the direct connection.
#
# CORE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# CORE_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# PRODUCTS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# PRODUCTS_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# TRANSACTIONS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# TRANSACTIONS_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# REPORTS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# REPORTS_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ---- Redis (Upstash) ----
# Upstash in every environment, addressed over TCP via a rediss:// URL.
# There is no local Redis container.
#
# REDIS_URL=rediss://default:PASSWORD@YOUR_REDIS_ENDPOINT.upstash.io:6379
